# PPS into the FC, logged as a camera feedback edge (coordinator#11)
#
# The 1 Hz from the DS3234 on the hub board is buffered and fanned out; one leg goes to
# an FC GPIO. AP_Camera_Backend's feedback ISR stamps each edge with a
# hardware-captured AP_HAL::micros64() and check_feedback() writes a CAM record,
# back-correcting the ISR-to-log delay. So every edge lands in the dataflash in the
# same clock the log stamps TimeUS with, beside the EKF state at that instant -- which
# is what ties a capture to a pose.
#
# No camera is involved and none is fitted.
#
# --- the pin ---
# Pad S11 = PE5 = GPIO(60). A real exposed pad; S5-S12 are all open on this board.
# TBS silkscreens servo pads "S" where ArduPilot's board page says "M", which is why
# earlier analysis read these as absent. S11/S12 are the TIM15 NODMA pair, so they are
# the least likely of the eight to be wanted for PWM later. PE5 is 5 V tolerant (FT)
# per the STM32H743xI pin table, which is moot while the buffer runs from 3.3 V.
#   provenance: flight-hardware, pads read off the board 2026-10-11
SERVO11_FUNCTION,-1
CAM1_FEEDBAK_PIN,60
#
# --- the edge ---
# 0 = TriggerLow = INTERRUPT_FALLING. The DEFAULT IS 1, which is the rising edge, and
# on a DS3234 that is the half second and the undriven RC edge: the datasheet says the
# output "transitions high 500ms after the seconds data transfer", and INT/SQW is
# open-drain so only the falling edge is driven. Falling is both the sharp edge and
# the top of the second.
#
# POL=0 also makes setup_feedback_callback() enable a pull-up, so the pin idles high.
# That is the wanted failure mode: with the coordinator off and the FC on battery the
# buffer output is unpowered, and a defined idle beats a floating pin inventing edges
# into an ISR.
CAM1_FEEDBAK_POL,0
#
# --- why a camera type at all ---
# AP_Camera::init() switches on the type and CameraType::NONE creates no backend, so
# there is no init(), no attach_interrupt and no ISR. Any non-zero type installs one.
# 5 = MAVLINK is the cheapest from source: it binds no pin, no relay and no servo
# output, and its trigger_pic() only broadcasts MAV_CMD_DO_DIGICAM_CONTROL, which with
# no camera present goes nowhere.
#
# This is NOT leftover config from a camera nobody can find. It exists to bring a
# backend into existence so the feedback ISR is installed.
#
# Cost: a CAM record every second, forever, in the dataflash.
CAM1_TYPE,5
